---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="FBLA vs DECA | Irvington FBLA" description="Comparing FBLA and DECA: Key differences, similarities, and how to choose the right business organization for you.">
	<section class="page-header">
		<div class="container">
			<h1>FBLA vs DECA</h1>
			<p>Which Business Organization is Right for You?</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="text-content">
				<h2>Overview</h2>
				<p>Both Future Business Leaders of America (FBLA) and DECA are premier student organizations that prepare students for careers in business. While they share similar goals, they have different focuses, competitive structures, and cultures. Many students at Irvington High School participate in both!</p>
				
				<h2>Key Differences</h2>
				
				<div class="comparison-table-wrapper">
					<table class="comparison-table">
						<thead>
							<tr>
								<th>Feature</th>
								<th>FBLA</th>
								<th>DECA</th>
							</tr>
						</thead>
						<tbody>
							<tr>
								<td><strong>Primary Focus</strong></td>
								<td>Broad business scope (Business, IT, Law, Finance, etc.)</td>
								<td>Marketing, Management, Hospitality, Finance</td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td><strong>Competition Style</strong></td>
								<td>Heavy on objective tests & production (computers); some role plays</td>
								<td>Heavy on role plays & case studies; some written exams</td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td><strong>Scope</strong></td>
								<td>Largest business CTSO in the world</td>
								<td>International focus with strong industry partnerships</td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td><strong>Eligibility</strong></td>
								<td>Open to middle school, high school, and college</td>
								<td>High school and college divisions</td>
							</tr>
						</tbody>
					</table>
				</div>

				<h2>Detailed Breakdown</h2>

				<h3>Future Business Leaders of America (FBLA)</h3>
				<p>FBLA is generally broader in scope. It covers everything from accounting and coding to public speaking and graphic design. If you prefer taking tests or creating projects (like websites, videos, or business plans) over impromptu speaking, FBLA might be a better fit. However, FBLA also has strong speaking and performance events.</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Best for:</strong> Students interested in a wide variety of business topics, technology/CS students, and those who like prepared projects or objective tests.</li>
				</ul>

				<h3>DECA</h3>
				<p>DECA focuses heavily on marketing, entrepreneurship, hospitality, and management. The core of DECA competitions involves "role plays" where you are given a business scenario and have a limited time to prepare a solution to present to a judge.</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Best for:</strong> Students who love public speaking, quick thinking, marketing, and sales.</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>Can I Join Both?</h2>
				<p><strong>Yes!</strong> At Irvington High School, many students are members of both FBLA and DECA. Joining both allows you to maximize your networking opportunities, gain a diverse set of skills, and compete in more events. However, be mindful of the time commitment required for both.</p>

				<h2>Conclusion</h2>
				<p>Both organizations are excellent for your resume and personal growth. We encourage you to explore both and see which one aligns best with your interests and strengths. Or better yet—join both and get the best of both worlds!</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>

